Capgemini | DevOps Interview Questions – 3–5 Years Experience 🚨

Recently asked DevOps interview questions that can help you prepare for your next Capgemini interview 👇

🔹 1. Kubernetes
👉 Explain Kubernetes Architecture.
👉 Explain the role of Control Plane, Worker Nodes, API Server, Scheduler, Controller Manager and etcd.

🔹 2. Kubernetes Deployment
👉 What is a Deployment in Kubernetes?
👉 What are the different deployment strategies?
👉 Write a Kubernetes Deployment YAML for an application.

🔹 3. Git – Rebase vs Merge
👉 What is the difference between git rebase and git merge?
👉 When would you prefer rebase over merge?

🔹 4. Git – Fetch vs Pull
👉 What is the difference between:
"git fetch" vs "git pull"
👉 What happens internally when you execute "git pull"?

🔹 5. Docker
👉 How can you create/save a Docker image from a running container?
💡 Example:
"docker commit <container_id> <image_name>:<tag>"

🔹 6. Ingress
👉 What is Ingress in Kubernetes?
👉 What is an Ingress Controller?
👉 How is Kubernetes Ingress different from a traditional ingress/load-balancing concept?

🔹 7. Jenkins
👉 What is a Jenkinsfile?
👉 How do you write a declarative Jenkins pipeline?
👉 Explain stages, agents, environment variables, parameters and post actions.

🔹 8. Docker Networking
👉 Explain Docker networking.
👉 What are the different Docker network drivers?
👉 How do containers communicate with each other?

🔹 9. Dockerfile – RUN vs CMD vs ENTRYPOINT
👉 What is the difference between:
• "RUN"
• "CMD"
• "ENTRYPOINT"

👉 Which one executes during image build and which one executes when the container starts?
